Input:
Design a Java class `TextEditor` that provides functionality for editing text. It should have methods for inserting and deleting text.

The class should also have a method `undo` that undoes the last edit (insertion or deletion) if there is one to undo, and a method `redo` that redoes the last undone edit if there is one to redo.

You may assume that the maximum number of undo operations is 100.
Output:

package com.example;

public class TextEditor {
    private String text = "";
    private int pointer = 0;
    private LinkedList<String> undoStack = new LinkedList<>();
    private LinkedList<String> redoStack = new LinkedList<>();

    public String getText() {
        return text;
    }

    public void insert(String textToInsert) {
        if (pointer == text.length()) {
            // Append at the end
            text += textToInsert;
        } else {
            text = text.substring(0, pointer) + textToInsert + text.substring(pointer);
        }
        pointer += textToInsert.length();
        undoStack.addFirst(text);
        redoStack.clear();
    }

    public void delete(int n) {
        int startIndex = Math.max(0, pointer - n);
        int endIndex = Math.min(text.length(), pointer);
        String deletedText = text.substring(startIndex, endIndex);
        text = text.substring(0, startIndex) + text.substring(endIndex);
        pointer = startIndex;
        undoStack.addFirst(text);
        redoStack.clear();
    }

    public void undo() {
        if (undoStack.isEmpty()) return;
        redoStack.addFirst(text);
        text = undoStack.removeLast();
        pointer = text.length();
    }

    public void redo() {
        if (redoStack.isEmpty()) return;
        text = redoStack.removeLast();
        undoStack.addFirst(text);
        pointer = text.length();
    }
}

